## Explorer search highlight survives a deferred first render

Context:
The search halo (8a91482b) was applied by a fixed 200 ms timer after
_expandAndRenderGraph called _render. On the first search after opening the
page _render defers itself until the entity groups load (or the container is
sized), so the timer ran before the graph existed, cleared the highlight and
never retried. The highlight also matched nodes by the search text instead of
the seed URIs the search returned, so type-only searches or text absent from
the label highlighted nothing.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
   - _expandAndRenderGraph records the seed URIs (_pendingHighlightSeeds)
     and clears the previous highlight; the 200 ms timer is removed.
   - _render calls _applyPendingHighlight right after the renderer exists,
     so deferred renders still get the highlight.
   - _applyPendingHighlight prefers seed URIs present in the graph and falls
     back to the term (reasoning highlights by term). With nothing pending it
     keeps the current highlight, so group toggles no longer drop it.
   - _clearGraphFilter / clearHighlight also clear the pending seeds.
2. tests/units/front/test_explorer_seed_halo.py
   New: no timer, applied from _render, URIs before the term, re-renders
   keep the highlight.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
- tests/units/front/test_explorer_seed_halo.py
- changelogs/v0.9.1/simyung-yang_2026-11-02.log

