uv run --frozen pytest -q tests/units/front -> 1808 passed.

## Deploy keeps the Lakebase endpoint at a configured compute

Context:
Lakebase compute was left at whatever the project was created with (1-4 CU
without scale-to-zero on some demo workspaces, 4-8 CU on others) and had to be
fixed by hand per workspace. The deploy config now owns it: every Lakebase
deploy sets the branch's read-write endpoint to 4-16 CU with scale-to-zero
after one hour, unless overridden.

Changes:
1. scripts/bootstrap/lakebase-compute.sh (new)
   Reads the read-write endpoint of projects/<project>/branches/<branch> and
   updates only the differing fields (autoscaling min/max CU, suspend
   timeout) with an update mask. Validates numbers, `Ns` timeouts and
   min <= max <= min + 16 before any API call. Empty values are left alone;
   --dry-run reports the change.
2. scripts/deploy.config.sh
   New DEFAULT_LAKEBASE_MIN_CU (4), DEFAULT_LAKEBASE_MAX_CU (16),
   DEFAULT_LAKEBASE_SUSPEND_TIMEOUT (3600s), exported as LAKEBASE_MIN_CU /
   LAKEBASE_MAX_CU / LAKEBASE_SUSPEND_TIMEOUT. "" opts a setting out.
3. scripts/deploy.sh
   New step "Apply Lakebase compute settings" right after the Lakebase
   project/database step (dry-run aware); the script is a required file.
4. docs/deployment.md
   Config table row for the three settings.
5. tests/units/scripts/test_lakebase_compute.py (new)
   Fake-CLI tests: update when different, no-op when equal, empty values,
   dry run, invalid input rejected before the API, config defaults, step order.

Modified files:
- scripts/bootstrap/lakebase-compute.sh
- scripts/deploy.config.sh
- scripts/deploy.sh
- docs/deployment.md
- tests/units/scripts/test_lakebase_compute.py
- changelogs/v0.9.1/simyung-yang_2026-11-02.log

